The IFD (Input Format Data) file structure currently consists of 8 data structures, these refer to the data attributes required for the BFT generated diagram for the following entities:

Nap, Fibre Bundle, Fibre Bundle Part, BFT, BFT Blocked Tubes, BFT Equipment, BFT Tubes and BFT Section.

The attributes defined for each are only those required for a BFT diagram and will need to be extended for other diagrams.  Their will be other entities added to the file definition as required by other diagrams.

The format of each record is very rigid and is not checked by GENGRAPH.EXE if it is not followed exactly, the results will be spurious.

The format of each entity follows the convention

Single Character identifier
'$' symbol
1st attribute
'$' symbol
2nd attribute
'$' symbol
Nth attribute
Carriage Return (0Dh)
Line Feed (0Ah)


Entity - NETWORK_ACCESS_POINT
Single Character Identifier N
	N$1$F$TU$T0001
Fibre Bundle
	F$50$8$1
Fibre Bundle Part
	P$19$100$1
BFT
	B$04$BFT4$ON
BFT Blocked Tubes
	U$14$5
BFT Equipment
	E$10$1$11$2$2
BFT Tubes
	T$BFT 7 PVC MK 2 5/3.5$7
BFT Section
	S$1$2$0$0$BFT 2 PE MK 2 5/3.5$BFT1$10$120

